==Serbo-Croatian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bêoɡrad/|lang=sh}}
* {{audio|Sr-beograd.ogg|audio}}

===Etymology===
Composed of [[Ekavian]] Serbo-Croatian {{term|бео|бе̏о|white|lang=sh|sc=Cyrl}} (< {{proto|Slavic|bělъ|lang=sh}}) and {{term|град|гра̑д|city|lang=sh|sc=Cyrl}} (< {{proto|Slavic|gordъ|lang=sh}}). The city is named after the white wall of the fortress that enclosed the city.

